<rml>
<head>
	<title>Dialogue</title>

	<!--
		A line of dialogue that types itself out.

		Copy into your own UI/screens/ and edit. The parts worth keeping:
		  - the line is a <text>, whose contents are Folio's markup rather than RML. `<angry>` is a
		    style, `{tag:}` is a name from UI/terms, `{delay:}` slows a stretch of it down. All of it
		    survives translation, because it is a string rather than elements
		  - one data-loc on the whole line. The markup is part of the string a translator receives,
		    and moving <angry> onto the word that carries the emphasis in their language is something
		    only they can do
		  - the feel is in the stylesheet. Rate, fade and pacing are inherited properties, so a game
		    tunes how its dialogue reads in one place rather than per line
		  - the continue prompt is a rule, not code: <text> carries .is-revealing while it types and
		    .is-revealed when it has finished, so the prompt appears on its own
		  - reveal-sound names a sound and plays nothing. The game hears about it through
		    FFolioModule::OnTextRevealSound and decides what that is
	-->
	<link type="text/template" href="/folio/lib/lib.rml"/>
	<meta name="folio-size" content="1280x720"/>

	<style>
		body {
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: column;
			justify-content: flex-end;
		}

		.box {
			width: 100%;
			border: 1dp #3a3a48;
			border-radius: 10dp;
		}

		.speaker { margin-bottom: 6dp; }

		/*
		 * How this game's dialogue reads. Every line inherits it, so this is the only place the
		 * pacing is decided.
		 *
		 * reveal-punctuation is the one worth playing with: without it an even stream of characters
		 * reads flat however well written the line is, and a beat after a full stop is most of what
		 * makes it sound like someone talking.
		 */
		.line {
			reveal: typewriter;
			reveal-rate: 45;
			reveal-fade: 0.08;
			reveal-rise: 2dp;
			reveal-punctuation: 0.18;
			reveal-sound: "dialogue-blip";
		}

		/* Nothing until the line has finished saying itself. */
		.continue {
			margin-top: 12dp;
			text-align: right;
			opacity: 0;
			transition: opacity 0.2s cubic-out;
		}

		.line.is-revealed ~ .continue { opacity: 1; }
	</style>
</head>

<body class="screen s-pad-xl">
	<div class="box c-surface s-pad-l e-2">
		<div class="speaker t-label c-accent" data-loc="speaker">Kaede</div>

		<text class="line t-body c-text" data-loc="line_1">You <angry>must</> go to the
			{tag:Place.Mountain.Temple}, I{delay:0.2}...{/} think?</text>

		<div class="continue t-caption c-dim" data-loc="continue">Continue</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
